  "source": "Comm-change reporting points populated from maintainer visual inspection of the printed IAA CVFR chart symbology ('נקודת מעבר קשר' — comm-transfer point legend), 2026-05-31, with a full waypoint tile audit follow-up on 2026-06-17. Call-sign frequency options are enriched from the maintainer-provided AirMapRadioFrequencies PDF generated 2026-06-06; assign available options per waypoint in points[].callSigns. Earlier desk-research sources (Israel eAIP 2025-10-02, PAMAT edition 1/24) did not yield OCR-extractable per-point data — see _NOTE.",
  "_definition": "Each entry marks a CVFR reporting point where pilots are expected to switch ATC frequencies because the point sits on (or at) a sector / CTR / TMA boundary. The chart annotation may be on the boundary line itself rather than directly at the point — the dataset records the *point of change*, not the chart-text position.",
  "_NOTE": "Reporting-type (חובה / דרישה — mandatory vs. on-request) is NOT comm-change and is tracked separately (PR #405). The points below come from maintainer inspection of the printed IAA CVFR chart's 'נקודת מעבר קשר' symbology, which supersedes the earlier citation bar that left this file empty. Points are matched to cvfr-nav-waypoints.json by 5-letter ICAO `name` only — never by Hebrew text.",
  "_frequencySource": "AirMapRadioFrequencies PDF, generated 2026-06-06",
  "_frequencySourceFile": "AirMapRadioFrequencies (1).pdf",
  "_militaryFrequencySource": "Maintainer-provided military unit / call-sign table, 2026-06-01",
  "_callSignsUsage": "Root callSigns is the reusable frequency catalog. Add call-sign ids to a comm-change waypoint's points[].callSigns array to expose those choices in the frequency-callout inspector. Optional points[].routeHints entries map route context to a call-sign id from that same point's callSigns array: before/after are adjacent route waypoint names around the comm-change point, and callSign is the suggested frequency owner. Labels/frequencies are derived from the catalog. The first id becomes the default; the frequency remains editable on the note.",
  "_TODO": [
    "Assign points[].callSigns per comm-change waypoint as each point is confirmed against the chart.",
    "Attach a public-document citation (IAA AIP supplement / PAMAT chapter B-03 page) per point where one exists, in the per-entry `source` field.",
    "Reporting-type data (mandatory / on-request) is tracked separately on the feat/reporting-required branch (PR #405) — DO NOT conflate the two datasets."
  ],
